<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.2.3: Radicals and Rational Exponents</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01260</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.2.3: Radicals and Rational Exponents</md:title>
    <md:uuid>41ff6169-7970-4598-8d7d-8a86e141d2f6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>If \(\sqrt[n]{a^m}\) is a real number and \(n\;\geq\;2\), then \(\sqrt[n]{a^m}\;=\;a^\frac mn\).</para>
<para>So radicals can be rewritten as rational exponents.</para>
<para>With a partner, write each radical as a term with rational exponents on your own paper. Then, turn and talk to your partner.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(\sqrt[8]x\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^\frac18\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(\sqrt[3]{x^2}\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^\frac23\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(\sqrt[11]{x^5}\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^\frac5{11}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><para>Now, with a partner, rewrite each term as an equivalent radical.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^\frac12\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\sqrt[2]x\;\) or \(\;\sqrt x\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^\frac17\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\sqrt[7]x\;\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^\frac45\) </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\sqrt[5]{x^4}\;\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><title>Video: Learning About Rational Exponents</title>
<para>Watch the following video to learn more about rational exponents.</para>
